## Library consumption (`npm run build`)

- **Output**: `dist/epds.js` (ESM), `dist/epds.css` (tokens + reset + extracted SFC styles), `dist/index.d.ts` (types). `public/` is not copied into `dist` for lib builds.
- **Peer dependency**: `vue` ^3.5 (see `package.json` `peerDependencies`).
- **Install in a host app**: `npm install epds` (when published) or `"epds": "file:../EPDS"` / workspace protocol for local monorepos — run `npm run build` in EPDS first so `dist/` exists.
- **Host app usage**:
  ```ts
  import { BaseButton, tokens } from 'epds'
  ```
  The package entry side-imports `epds.css`; bundlers should emit/load `dist/epds.css` automatically. Load **Roboto** (300/400/500/700) in the host app the same way as `index.html` / Storybook preview-head.
- **App shell vs library**: `npm run build` writes **`dist/`** (publish this for npm). `npm run build:app` writes **`dist-app/`** so it never overwrites the library output; use `vite preview` after `build:app` if you need to check the shell. Storybook is unchanged (`npm run storybook` / `build-storybook`).
- **New components**: add a barrel under `src/components/Name/` and register the export in `src/index.ts` (plus any public types already exported from the component `index.ts`).

## CI & GitHub Pages

- **`npm run build`** runs **`vue-tsc -p tsconfig.lib.json --noEmit`** then **`vite build --config vite.lib.config.ts`** — verifies typings and emits **`dist/epds.js`**, **`dist/epds.css`**, **`dist/index.d.ts`**. Dependencies must exist locally (`npm ci` / `npm install`).
- **`.github/workflows/ci.yml`** — on every **push** and **pull request** targeting **`main`**: `npm ci` → **`npm run build`**. Confirms the **library** stays buildable on clean CI (orthogonal to docs).
- **`.github/workflows/deploy-storybook.yml`** — on **push** to **`main`** (plus **workflow_dispatch**): `npm ci` → **`npm run build-storybook`** → uploads **`storybook-static`** → **GitHub Pages** (`STORYBOOK_BASE=/EPDS/` for the `/EPDS/` site path).
- **npm publish** / registry releases are **not** automated here; workflows **verify** the lib build and **host** Storybook only.

## TypeScript & tooling notes

- **`tsconfig.app.json`** extends **`./node_modules/@vue/tsconfig/tsconfig.dom.json`** (relative path so editors resolve the Vue baseline even when package-style `@vue/tsconfig/...` `extends` is flaky).
- **`src/vite-env.d.ts`**: keep **`/// <reference types="vite/client" />`**. Declare **`declare module '*?url' { … }`** so multi-segment URL imports typecheck (e.g. `@logos/OEMs/Audi.svg?url`) — Vite's default **`*.svg?url`** patterns only match a single path segment.
- **Strict unused locals**: `vue-tsc` honours **`noUnusedLocals`** from the TS config chain — remove unused script symbols (stub helpers that are never wired to the template) or the lib build fails.
